"samutkrīḍā (EI 15), same as krīḍā or sport.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samva": [{"id": "samva", "headword": "सम्व", "headword_slp1": "samva", "fold": "samva", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samva (IE 8-1), mistake for saṃva which is an abbreviation of saṃvatsara.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samvat": [{"id": "samvat", "headword": "सम्वत्", "headword_slp1": "samvat", "fold": "samvat", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samvat (IE 8-1), mistake for saṃvat, originally an abbreviation of saṃvatsara.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samvata": [{"id": "samvatta", "headword": "सम्वत्त", "headword_slp1": "samvatta", "fold": "samvata", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samvatta (IE 8-1), corrupt form of saṃvat.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samvatu": [{"id": "samvatu", "headword": "सम्वतु", "headword_slp1": "samvatu", "fold": "samvatu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samvatu, samvatū (IE 8-1), corrupt forms of saṃvat.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samya": [{"id": "sAmya", "headword": "साम्य", "headword_slp1": "sAmya", "fold": "samya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sāmya (EI 23), often written for svāmya; cf. leja-sāmya standing for tejaḥ-svāmya.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["साम्यं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["sAmyaM"]}], "samyakpraDana": [{"id": "samyakpraDAna", "headword": "सम्यक्प्रधान", "headword_slp1": "samyakpraDAna", "fold": "samyakpraDana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samyak-pradhāna, cf. sammappadhāna (EI 5), Buddhist; four in number.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samaDukacutavanavawikaviwapatfnayutigocaraparyanta": [{"id": "samaDUkacUtavanavAwikAviwapatfnayUtigocaraparyanta", "headword": "समधूकचूतवनवाटिकाविटपतृनयूतिगोचरपर्यन्त", "headword_slp1": "samaDUkacUtavanavAwikAviwapatfnayUtigocaraparyanta", "fold": "samaDukacutavanavawikaviwapatfnayutigocaraparyanta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sa-madhūka-cūta-vana-vāṭikā-viṭapa-tṛna-yūti-gocara-paryanta , ‘together with the madhūka and mango trees, forests, gardens, bushes (or, branches), grass yūti (grass land) and including the pasture land’; cf. Ind. Ep., p. 396. It is better to take sa-madhūka-cūṭa-vana-vāṭikā-viṭapa and tṛnayūti-gocara-paryanta separately.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samaDukamravanavawikaviwapatfRayutigocaraparyanta": [{"id": "samaDUkAmravanavAwikAviwapatfRayUtigocaraparyanta", "headword": "समधूकाम्रवनवाटिकाविटपतृणयूतिगोचरपर्यन्त", "headword_slp1": "samaDUkAmravanavAwikAviwapatfRayUtigocaraparyanta", "fold": "samaDukamravanavawikaviwapatfRayutigocaraparyanta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sa-madhūk-āmra-vana-vāṭikā-viṭapa-tṛṇa-yūti-gocara-paryanta (EI 24), ‘together with the madhuka and mango trees, forests, gardens, shrubs and as far as and the grass yuli (grass land) and pasture lands’. See sa-madhūka-cūta … , above.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samandiraprakara": [{"id": "samandiraprAkAra", "headword": "समन्दिरप्राकार", "headword_slp1": "samandiraprAkAra", "fold": "samandiraprakara", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sa-mandira-prākāra , ‘together with temples and walls’; epithet of gift village. Cf. Ind. Ep., p. 395. [] trees and areas covered by jungles (or areas covered with mango and madhūka plantations)’; see Ind. Ep., p. 402.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samaYcamahakaraRa": [{"id": "samaYcamahAkaraRa", "headword": "समञ्चमहाकरण", "headword_slp1": "samaYcamahAkaraRa", "fold": "samaYcamahakaraRa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sa-mañca-mahākaraṇa (EI 26), ‘together with mañca (probably, platforms for the collection of tolls) and mahākaraṇa (official documents)’; epithet of the gift land.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samantamatyadutanam": [{"id": "sAmantAmAtyadUtAnAm", "headword": "सामन्तामात्यदूतानाम्", "headword_slp1": "sAmantAmAtyadUtAnAm", "fold": "samantamatyadutanam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sāmant-āmātya-dūtānām=anyeṣām c=ābhyupāgame śayanīy-āsana-siddhānnaṃ na dāpayet , refers to the obligation of the people to supply beds, seats and boiled or unboiled rice to feudatory rulers, ministers, messengers and others encamped in a village; see a-kūra-cullaka-vināśi-khaṭv-āvāsa, etc. See Ep. Ind., Vol. XXX, p. 171.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samastaBagaBogakarahiraRyadipratyayasameta": [{"id": "samastaBAgaBogakarahiraRyAdipratyAyasameta", "headword": "समस्तभागभोगकरहिरण्यादिप्रत्यायसमेत", "headword_slp1": "samastaBAgaBogakarahiraRyAdipratyAyasameta", "fold": "samastaBagaBogakarahiraRyadipratyayasameta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samasta-bhāga-bhoga-kara-hiraṇy-ādi-pratyāya-sameta , ‘together with all incomes including the king's grain share, the periodical offerings to be made to the king or landlord and to the touring officers, taxes in grains, taxes in cash, etc.’; epithet of gift land; same as sa-hiraṇya-bhāga-bhoga, etc. See Ind. Ep., p. 397.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samastaBagaBogakarahiraRyadayasameta": [{"id": "samastaBAgaBogakarahiraRyAdAyasameta", "headword": "समस्तभागभोगकरहिरण्यादायसमेत", "headword_slp1": "samastaBAgaBogakarahiraRyAdAyasameta", "fold": "samastaBagaBogakarahiraRyadayasameta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samasta-bhāga-bhoga-kara-hiraṇy-ādāya-sameta (EI 23), same as sa-hiraṇya-bhāga-bhoga, etc.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samastarajakiyanam": [{"id": "samastarAjakIyAnAm", "headword": "समस्तराजकीयानाम्", "headword_slp1": "samastarAjakIyAnAm", "fold": "samastarajakiyanam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samasta-rājakīyānām=apraveśya , same as a-bhaṭa-praveśa, a-cāṭa-bhaṭa-praveśya, a-bhaṭa-cchātra-prāveśya, etc. (Ind. Ep., p. 398).", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "samastarAjakIyAnam", "headword": "समस्तराजकीयानम्", "headword_slp1": "samastarAjakIyAnam", "fold": "samastarajakiyanam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samasta-rājakīyānam=ahasta-prakṣepaṇīya (CII 3), same as ā-bhaṭa-praveśa, etc.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samastarajapratyadayasameta": [{"id": "samastarAjapratyAdAyasameta", "headword": "समस्तराजप्रत्यादायसमेत", "headword_slp1": "samastarAjapratyAdAyasameta", "fold": "samastarajapratyadayasameta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samasta-rājapratyādāya-sameta (Ep. Ind., Vol. XXXV, p. 129), same as sa-hiraṇya-bhāga-bhoga, etc.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samastotpatisahita": [{"id": "samastotpattisahita", "headword": "समस्तोत्पत्तिसहित", "headword_slp1": "samastotpattisahita", "fold": "samastotpatisahita", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samast-otpatti-sahita (EI 12), ‘together with all the produce or income’.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samastotpatisulkotpatisahita": [{"id": "samastotpattiSulkotpattisahita", "headword": "समस्तोत्पत्तिशुल्कोत्पत्तिसहित", "headword_slp1": "samastotpattiSulkotpattisahita", "fold": "samastotpatisulkotpatisahita", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samast-otpatti-śulk-otpatti-sahita (EI 23), ‘together with all the produce of the land and the income arising from tolls’.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samatsyakacCapa": [{"id": "samatsyakacCapa", "headword": "समत्स्यकच्छप", "headword_slp1": "samatsyakacCapa", "fold": "samatsyakacCapa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sa-matsya-kacchapa (EI 12), ‘together with the right to catch fish and tortoises’; epithet of gift village.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samatsyakara": [{"id": "samatsyAkara", "headword": "समत्स्याकर", "headword_slp1": "samatsyAkara", "fold": "samatsyakara", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sa-matsy-ākara (EI 24), 26), ‘together with the sources of fish (e. g., rivers, tanks, etc)’; epithet of gift village.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samhalalamakasamanvita": [{"id": "samhalAlamakasamanvita", "headword": "सम्हलालमकसमन्वित", "headword_slp1": "samhalAlamakasamanvita", "fold": "samhalalamakasamanvita", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samhalātamaka-samanvita (EI 9), the reading is apparently wrong; meaning uncertain.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "saminatoya": [{"id": "samInatoya", "headword": "समीनतोय", "headword_slp1": "samInatoya", "fold": "saminatoya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sa-mīna-toya (EI 24), ‘together with fish and the waters’ or ‘together with the waters containing fish.’", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samramaDuka": [{"id": "sAmramaDUka", "headword": "साम्रमधूक", "headword_slp1": "sAmramaDUka", "fold": "samramaDuka", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "s-āmra-madhūka (IE; EI 12, 27, 29), ‘together with the mango and madhūka trees’.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samramaDuvana": [{"id": "sAmramaDuvana", "headword": "साम्रमधुवन", "headword_slp1": "sAmramaDuvana", "fold": "samramaDuvana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "s-āmra-madhu-vana (EI 12), same as s-āmra-madhū-van-ākīrṇa.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samramaDuvanakirRa": [{"id": "sAmramaDuvanAkIrRa", "headword": "साम्रमधुवनाकीर्ण", "headword_slp1": "sAmramaDuvanAkIrRa", "fold": "samramaDuvanakirRa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "s-āmra-madhu-van-ākīrṇa , see Ind. Ep., p. 402.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samrapanasa": [{"id": "sAmrapanasa", "headword": "साम्रपनस", "headword_slp1": "sAmrapanasa", "fold": "samrapanasa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "s-āmra-panasa (EI 12), ‘together with mango and jack trees’.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samuCitadeyaBagaBogakarahiraRyadi": [{"id": "samuCitadeyaBAgaBogakarahiraRyAdi", "headword": "समुछितदेयभागभोगकरहिरण्यादि", "headword_slp1": "samuCitadeyaBAgaBogakarahiraRyAdi", "fold": "samuCitadeyaBagaBogakarahiraRyadi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samucita-deya-bhāga-bhoga-kara-hiraṇy-ādi (EI 23), same as sa-hiraṇya-bhāga-bhoga, etc.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samudayabahyadyastamba": [{"id": "samudayabAhyAdyastamba", "headword": "समुदयबाह्याद्यस्तम्ब", "headword_slp1": "samudayabAhyAdyastamba", "fold": "samudayabahyadyastamba", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "samudayabāhy-ādyastamba (EI 23), ‘[land] covered with original shrubs (i. e. never cultivated) and not yielding any revenue [to the State].’", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "samula": [{"id": "samUla", "headword": "समूल", "headword_slp1": "samUla", "fold": "samula", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sa-mūla (EI 13), ‘together with the root crops’.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["समूलं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["samUlaM"]}], "sambiraRipalaNgasu": [{"id": "sambiraRippalaNgASu", "headword": "सम्बिरणिप्पलङ्गाशु", "headword_slp1": "sambiraRippalaNgASu", "fold": "sambiraRipalaNgasu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sambiraṇippalaṅ-gāśu , see kāśu.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "same": [{"id": "same", "headword": "समे", "headword_slp1": "same", "fold": "same", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "Same as Sthān-ācārya (EI 17), a temple priest.\n (EI 8; IA 14), an architect; used in the sense of ‘a master’, i. e. ‘a master-mason’; cf. Ācāri (EI 17), an artisan. Pāli Ācariya is explained as ‘a master goldsmith’ in the P. T. S.Pāli-Eng. Dict.\n (HA; IA 19), Jain; a Sādhu who has the right of both reading the sacred texts publicly and explaining them authoritatively.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Same as paṭṭaka (q.v.); cf. Paṭṭa-lekhin, etc.\n (ASLV), an account book. []\n (LP), abbreviation of Paṭṭadhara; probably one who has the charter for collecting government revenues; cf. Paṭṭakila.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Same as paṭṭa; cf. rāja-paṭṭī (EI 4).", "gloss_language": "en"}]}]}